            'value' => 'the API below `<dashboard-path>/api/v1`: `api` on (default) or off; `api-write` on for the endpoints that change something (off by default); `api-origins` the websites whose pages may call it from a browser (CORS) ([the API](RSF06-05-api.md))'],
        ['keys' => ['http-cache', 'http-cache-hosts', 'http-cache-ttl', 'http-cache-cookies', 'http-cache-max-object', 'http-cache-memory-object', 'http-cache-memory', 'http-cache-disk', 'http-cache-dir', 'http-cache-purgers', 'http-cache-purge-token', 'http-cache-tag-headers', 'http-cache-session-cookie', 'http-cache-context-ttl', 'http-cache-user-context', 'http-cache-user-hash-header'],
            'label' => '`http-cache`, `http-cache-hosts`, `http-cache-ttl`, `http-cache-cookies`, `http-cache-max-object`, `http-cache-memory-object`, `http-cache-memory`, `http-cache-disk`, `http-cache-dir`, `http-cache-purgers`, `http-cache-purge-token`, `http-cache-tag-headers`, `http-cache-session-cookie`, `http-cache-context-ttl`, `http-cache-user-context`, `http-cache-user-hash-header`',
            'value' => 'the HTTP cache: `http-cache` on or off (default); how long an answer is kept when it says nothing (`5m`); the cookies that do not make a page someone\'s own (default: analytics, the pass); the largest answer kept (`1M`); with APCu the largest kept in memory (`256K`, `0`: none) and the most of APCu the answers may take (`32M`); the most the folder holds, the oldest going first (`256M`, at least `1M`; `0`: no cap); where (default `<store-dir>/http-cache`); who may purge with a request (`PURGE`, `PURGEKEYS`; default: nobody -- `127.0.0.1 ::1` for a CMS on this machine), or anyone with this `X-Invalidate-Token`; a tag header besides the known ones; the session cookies a page per role is kept for, and how long a session\'s role is remembered (`10m`); the role from FOSHttpCache\'s user hash without an adapter (`on`, or the address to ask; off by default) and its header (`X-User-Context-Hash`, `X-User-Hash` for Exponential Platform) ([the HTTP cache](RSF04-03-http-cache.md))'],
        ['keys' => ['cache-unknown-query'], 'label' => '`cache-unknown-query`',
            'value' => 'a parameter `cache-query` does not name: `uncached` (default: the page is made, never kept) or `hit-only` (answered from the kept page without it, never kept -- `$_SERVER[\'REQUEST_SHIELD_CACHE_LOOKUP\']` names that page for a PHP cache) ([the cacheable definition](RSF04-01-cacheable-definition.md#query-parameters-in-the-key-ignored-unknown))'],
        ['keys' => ['file-mode', 'dir-mode'], 'label' => '`file-mode`, `dir-mode`',
            'value' => 'the modes of the files and folders the shield makes -- store-dir and what is in it, the log, the statistics, the lists, the feeds, the HTTP cache: `0600` and `0700` by default (only the user PHP runs as); a server\'s own rules exactly (`0640`/`0750` for a group, `02770` so the group is inherited) -- set with chmod after making, before any data, the umask takes nothing away; never writable for everyone; above the site blocks. What exists keeps its mode; the secret and the compiled settings stay `0600` ([settings](RSF05-02-settings.md#file-and-folder-modes))'],
        ['keys' => ['stats'], 'label' => '`stats`',
            'value' => '`off` (default), `on`, or the parts: `requests`, `crawlers`, `not-found`, `bots`, `pages`, `forms` (what `on` counts), and `times` -- how long the site took, only when named ([statistics](RSF06-03-statistics.md))'],
        ['keys' => ['stats-slow'], 'label' => '`stats-slow`',
            'value' => 'with `stats … times`: a request slower than this goes to the slow log (`2s` by default, `0` none) -- a line each, page and time, no address ([how fast the site answered](RSF06-03-statistics.md#how-fast-the-site-answered))'],
        ['keys' => ['dashboard-path'], 'label' => '`dashboard-path`',
            'value' => 'where the statistics pages live: `/rs` (default) gives the statistics under `/rs/stats/` (`overview`, `visitors`, `protection`, `sites`) and `/rs/waf/rules`, `/rs/waf/live`, `/rs/waf/lists`; something in front is fine (`/admin/rs`); the shield serves these pages itself -- a `restrict` rule (`restrict **/rs/** to <addresses>`) or a login must cover them, `check` warns otherwise ([statistics](RSF06-03-statistics.md#the-statistics-page))'],
        ['keys' => ['stats-hours', 'stats-days', 'stats-months', 'stats-flush'], 'label' => '`stats-hours`, `stats-days`, `stats-months`, `stats-flush`',
            'value' => 'days the hours are kept (7), days the day totals are kept (400, then summed into months), months kept (0: for good), seconds between writes to disk with APCu (60)'],
        ['keys' => ['site-from'], 'label' => '`site-from`',
